---

= Instructions

Combine all ingredients in a blender with 6 oz of pebble @Ice{}: @Planteray 3 Stars{1 1/2 oz} (or white rum), 
@El Dorado 8{1/2 oz} (or aged rum), @Appleton Signature{1/2 oz} (or Jamaican rum), @Key lime juice{3/4 oz},
@Pineapple juice{1 oz}, @Graham Cracker Syrup*{1 oz}, @Key Lime Pie Mix*{1 oz}, 
@Bittermens Elemakule tiki bitters{8 drops}, @Saline solution (20%){8 drops}.

Briefly flash blend until just incorporated and chilled.

Open pour into a #Pilsner glass{}.

Top off with additional pebble @Ice{} to fill the glass.

Garnish with a @Mint{} bouquet and an @Orchid{}.

> Graham Cracker Syrup:\
Gently crush 9 full graham cracker sheets (36 individual rectangles, roughly 135 grams)
and toast in a pan over medium-low heat for 5 minutes until browning starts and they become fragrant.
Remove from heat and add to 12 oz water.
Allow to infuse for 45 minutes before passing through a fine sieve lined with cheesecloth to remove solids.
Weigh out weight of graham cracker water in grams, then combine in a saucepan with an equal weight of cane sugar,
1/2 tsp vanilla extract, a pinch of ground cinnamon, and a pinch of salt.
Heat on low just until sugar is dissolved. Remove from heat, allow to cool and bottle.
Keep refrigerated and shake before using. 

> Key Lime Pie Mix:\
Combine 6 oz sweetened condensed milk, 6 oz coconut milk,
and 3 teaspoons freshly grated key lime zest. Whisk vigorously to combine,
then store in refrigerator for 4 hours. Pour through a fine sieve to remove zest and bottle.
Keep refrigerated and shake before using.